## Environment Variables Setup

#### BACKEND AUTH0
BACKEND_AUTH0_DOMAIN=your-tenant.auth0.com
BACKEND_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here
BACKEND_AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET=your_secret_here  
BACKEND_AUTH0_API_AUDIENCE=https://your-api.example.com
BACKEND_AUTH0_M2M_CLIENT_ID=your_m2m_client_id
BACKEND_AUTH0_M2M_CLIENT_SECRET=your_m2m_secret

#### FRONTEND AUTH0
FRONTEND_AUTH0_SECRET=generate_using_openssl_rand_hex_32
FRONTEND_AUTH0_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
FRONTEND_AUTH0_ISSUER_BASE_URL=https://your-tenant.auth0.com
FRONTEND_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID=your_frontend_client_id

#### DATABASE - POSTGRES
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_NAME=kaban_dev
DB_USER=postgres
DB_PASSWORD=your_secure_password

#### EMAIL SERVICE - BREVO
BREVO_API_KEY=your_brevo_api_key_here
BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL=noreply@example.com

#### REDIS
REDIS_HOST=localhost
REDIS_PORT=6379
REDIS_DB=0
REDIS_PASSWORD=
REDIS_USE_SSL=false

#### TERRAFORM VARIABLES
# Tis will be used as staging.tfvars in te terraform/environment/staging when we want to apply 'terraform plan -var-file="staging.tfvars" -out=tfplan' or added to github repo secret
# Add to: Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions
# - AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET
# - AUTH0_M2M_CLIENT_SECRET
# - AUTH0_SECRET
# - BREVO_API_KEY
# Note: DB_PASSWORD and REDIS_PASSWORD are auto-generated by Terraform